# Alpha frontend environment template.
#
# `make config` copies this to `frontend/.env` on first setup. Every value here
# is optional: the defaults below are what the code already uses, so an empty
# `.env` is a working configuration. Copy a line and uncomment it only when you
# need to override a default.
#
# This file is tracked; `frontend/.env` is gitignored. Do not put a real secret
# here — anything in a `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable is inlined into the client
# bundle and is visible to every browser.

# Base URL of the Gateway API, as seen by the browser.
#
# Leave this unset when you reach Alpha through the bundled Nginx entry point
# (http://localhost:2026): the same-origin default of "/api" is correct, because
# Nginx proxies /api/* to the Gateway.
#
# Set it only when the browser must reach the Gateway directly — for example
# `pnpm dev` on port 3000 without Nginx in front, which is when the Gateway has
# to be addressed by absolute origin. An absolute value is normalised to end in
# /api, so both forms below are equivalent:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8001
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=/api
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=

# Secret used by the frontend's own session layer. It must match the Gateway's
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET for browser sign-in to work. Use a value from your root
# .env; do not invent a second one.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=local-dev-secret
